{
    "background_story": "In ancient Greek mythology, Myla was a mystical herm, a creature with the upper body of a beautiful maiden and the lower body of a sturdy pillar. She was said to possess the power to communicate with the gods and mortals alike. Myla stood guard at the crossroads of the city, offering guidance and wisdom to those who sought it. Her presence was a beacon of hope and protection, and people would often leave offerings of flowers and honey at her base. According to legend, Myla's pillar-body was rooted deep within the earth, connecting her to the ancient secrets of the land. Her gentle voice and compassionate heart made her a beloved figure, and her wisdom was sought by kings and commoners alike.",
